{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Interaction"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag"}]}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into